"base": "main", "title": "Fix round_money to use banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN) per FIN-212", "body": "`src/money.py` said in its docstring that it used banker's rounding (ROUND_HALF_EVEN, per FIN-212), but the code actually used `ROUND_HALF_UP`. That broke `tests/test_money.py::test_half_even`, which made the nightly build fail.\n\nThis PR switches `round_money` to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN`.\n\nCI: run ci-0001 on 08d3cd5986 passed.\n\nNote: `wait_for_ci` returned a failed result for a different run (main@0c0ffee000, flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals`). That isn't related to this change, but main may have a flaky ledger test.", "reviewers": ["alex"], "idempotency_key": "pr-fix-money-banker-rounding"}, "name": "open_pr", "type": "tool_use", "toolset_name": null}]}, {"stop_reason": "end_turn", "content": [{"citations": null, "text": "I fixed the rounding bug, CI passed, and PR #101 is open against main with alex as reviewer: https://git.example/payments-service/pull/101\n\n- **The bug:** `round_money` in `src/money.py` used `ROUND_HALF_UP`, even though its own docstring says it uses banker's rounding (`ROUND_HALF_EVEN`, per FIN-212). That's why `test_half_even` failed in the nightly build. I changed it to `ROUND_HALF_EVEN` on a new branch, `fix/money-banker-rounding`.\n- **CI:** Run ci-0001 on my commit (`08d3cd5986`) passed. The wait tool first came back with a failure, but that result was from a different run: a flaky `tests/test_ledger.py::test_totals` on main (`0c0ffee000`). Checking the run status directly and listing the runs for my branch both showed a pass. I mentioned this in the PR description, since main may have a flaky ledger test.\n- **FIN-212:** The advisory lookup tool didn't recognise this ID, so I couldn't check the policy itself. The fix is based on the test and the code's docstring.\n\nI haven't merged the PR, because merging into main needs code-owner approval.", "type": "text"}]}]}